00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.230 align:start position:0%
 
there are some huge changes coming to  overwatch too from new heroes and  mechanics to a whole new free-to-play  model we're gonna round up all the big  news as well as hear straight from the  game's director aaron keller about what  we can expect when overwatch 2 launches  on october 4th  obviously one of the biggest changes is  that overwatch 2 will be going free to  play when we asked aaron why the answer  was pretty simple it keeps the player  base together rather than releasing  another box that players would have to  buy in order to opt into the experience  we'd rather open the game to as a broad  of a population as possible so overwatch  is a game of teamwork and cooperation  and strategy and and we feel like it's  played best in a social setting or with  your friends and so removing that  barrier to entry  um the the at the price is a barrier to  entry is hopefully a way for you to be  able to play with more of your friends  and have a better experience with the  game  on top of that just like in overwatch  one there's cross platform play which  will be enabled in the game's second  beta which will be on xbox playstation  and pc at the end of june if you're  going to be playing overwatch 2 on a  different platform than you played  overwatch 1 have no fear there's cross  platform progression 2. details on how  that will work are thin on the ground  right now but as someone who has to have  a playstation overwatch account and a pc  one i can't wait to finally bring all my  unlocks together into one game over the  past couple of years overwatch has  definitely had a content problem yes  there's been timed events and regular  competitive seasons but the last new  hero was echo and she launched over two  years ago with overwatch 2 becoming free  to play the team are being more  transparent with players changing how  they approach releasing new content and  making sure there are enough frequent  updates to keep players coming back each  overwatch 2 season will last about 9  weeks and there'll be a new hero every  other season you heard that right the  drought is over each season will  apparently have more content than the  team has ever shipped seasonally before  so brace yourselves there'll be new  heroes maps game modes events features  and even systems in order to make it all  the overwatch team is now three times  the size it used to be let's delve into  that road map then season one kicks off  on october 4th and there'll be three new  heroes junker queen sojourn and a  mysterious third who is an unannounced  support hero there'll be six new maps we  saw four in the first beta and a new one  is coming in the next there'll be a  battle pass and by the way overwatch 2  will have a battle pass model and  there'll be 30 plus new skins a new game  mode and a new mythic skin but more on  that later  season 2 will launch on december 6th and  will include a new tank hero new math 30  plus new skins new battle pass and a new  mythic skin  leveling up in overwatch 2 won't net you  that sweet sweet loot box anymore when  we asked aaron why he had this to say  loot boxes they've always been a part of  overwatch one but as the game has grown  and especially as we go into a  free-to-play version of the game where  we're adding more and more cosmetics  it becomes a lot harder to earn what you  want with a loot box system and so um by  losing those and moving over to a shop  for overwatch 2 it gives players the  actual agency and the choice to go after  what it is they want to have in the game  you can earn certain unlockables through  the game's battle pass but you can also  buy things from the in-game shop in  addition to classic unlocks like skins  voice lines and sprays they'll also be  new items like weapon charms and mythic  skins which are basically a cut above a  legendary skin for one mythic skins are  customizable season one's mythic skin  will be genji and according to aaron you  can swap out his tattoos change their  colors and check out the visual effects  added to his mask there'll be a new  mythic skin with every season earlier  this year blizzard revealed that the pve  was being decoupled from the multiplayer  part of overwatch 2 and questions have  been swirling on how exactly the  campaign content will work well we  finally have an answer and know why that  model changed when we  initially announced overwatch 2  we presented a vision of a pvp  game that  had a big pve component to it at the  same time  and as we developed that game  what it meant was that the pvp side of  the game was coupled or was joined with  the pve side of the game and so the  release of any pvp content was now being  gated by the amount of time it took for  us to to build the pve side of the game  and as that took longer it meant that  there was less focus going in to the  live side of the game  and  this i feel like this went against one  of the core values that the overwatch  team has always had which is to be able  to deliver content regularly for our  players and so the longer that went i  think we realized that  we had to change something  and so i understand that that there was  a vision of what overwatch 2 was but we  are changing that and the reason that we  are changing that is because we want to  be able to get content to our players as  soon as we possibly can we think that  that is the right thing to do for our  community we think it's the right thing  to do for the game it's the right thing  to do for all of our players and so that  was the initial  impetus of what caused us to to  completely  change our strategy overwatch 2 is going  to have a full aaa campaign with a  linear story and a replayable mode  that'll include hero progression instead  of releasing those separately they'll  launch as part of overwatch 2's seasonal  cadence starting in 2023 the pve  differentiates massively from pvp  because progression is tied to each hero  as you level them up they can gain more  talent and equipment we've heard about a  few of these new abilities like tracer  being able to damage enemies by blinking  through them and reinhardt being able to  gain armor when his barrier breaks  they'll be talking more about pve closer  to its rollout the 34th hero coming to  overwatch is junker queen a new tank  hero who will be playable in the  upcoming june beta not only does she  look let's face it  amazing but she actually brings new  mechanics to overwatch i'll let aaron  break it down she utilizes a mechanic  called bleed  and when she does certain types of  damage to characters she receives  that same amount  as overhealth to her and there's lots of  different ways for her to do it and she  fights with an axe  a dagger and she uses this like  electromagnetic gauntlet to control some  of this so when she throws her dagger  out she can then reactivate the ability  and pull it back  and it will pull it will like  pierce everybody that's in the way of it  so you can hit somebody on the way out  and pull it back and do damage to them  again or sometimes you can purposefully  miss  and put it behind a team and then pull  it back through them  hitting each one of them applying a  bleed to each one of them and taking all  of that as overhealth  also when she swings her axe when she  cleaves with it  she can take all of that damage and  apply a bleed and get that as over  health as well so if she's playing right  and hitting people frequently she's able  to be really tanky and kind of just stay  up in front of people and on top of that  she has a buff where she shouts  and she gives basically a haste  as well as over health to to herself as  well as all of her allies and so she's  one of these tanks that um she might not  be she's not long range but when she's  in the thick of things and when she's  hitting people she's really really hard  to take down the overwatch team also  debuted a new map for pvp called paraiso  the map is set in rio which means lucio  fans will find a lot to love about it  especially because the last third of the  map actually takes place in lucio's club  and the defending team spawns in his  home one of my favorite things about  busan is that you get to see diva's  space so i'm really hoping lucio's home  is packed full of easter eggs in terms  of the map itself it's a hybrid one so  the attacking team will need to capture  a point and then escort a payload  through the rest of the map in terms of  what characters will excel on this map  it's all about mobility baby there's  high ground all around the first point  and each team has a different way to  access it so defense can kind of access  high ground from their side of the point  and offense has a few ways of accessing  it from their side and so there's um a  lot of use for highly mobile characters  on on this map and then as you move  through um and get towards the end um  the the high ground actually continues  um and so there's as you travel through  this um sort of like more quaint village  section of rio there's different  rooftops that you can get to there's  different levels of lucio's club that  you can get to um and i think that it's  like it's a really fun  map that really highlights a lot of our  heroes movement abilities um as well as  a lot of the um sort of like long range  sight lines that we have while still  providing all these like tight little  flanking routes for heroes like reaper  um and um  i was gonna say junker queen  and junker queen to excel on  paraiso will be playable in the june  beta but if that wasn't enough we also  caught a glimpse of another new map  called portugal i've got some sneaky  footage of it right here looks like it's  another push map to go with the new game  mode that we'll be debuting with  overwatch 2.  as a huge overwatch fan honestly the new  changes have me very excited  we have been kept starving of overwatch  content for the past couple of years and  the promise of at least the first year  and beyond already being mapped out with  new heroes and maps and modes is  incredibly incredibly exciting and it  makes me want to delve back in it  obviously remains to be seen how the  micro transactions will work now that we  don't have loot boxes anymore and if the  battle pass is going to be satisfying  every season but i guess we'll have to  wait and see to find out if you want to  see more from our interview with aaron  keller make sure to subscribe to the  channel we'll be posting it shortly and  for more on overwatch 2 make sure to  stay tuned to gamespot

